message: "If you use these submission packages, please cite them as below."
title: "AB-Cloud Research Programme: Journal Submission Deliverables (NSR JINR, SciPost Physics, arXiv preprint)"
authors:
  - family-names: "Isaev"
    given-names: "Iskhak Khamzatovich"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-7299-0701"
date-released: "2026-10-18"
repository-code: "https://github.com/wild8highlander/ab-cloud-research/tree/main/AB_Cloud_Academic_Package/Journal"
abstract: >-
  The sealed, venue-tailored submission packages of the AB-Cloud research
  programme, compiled from the unified academic edition. Three packages:
  NSR (JINR) - full manuscript (100 pp.) on the official nsr.cls v1.5 class
  with cover letter, 48 figures and supplemental material (code + run data);
  SciPost Physics - Publication version (60 pp.) plus a condensed Core
  version (11 pp.) on the official SciPost.cls; arXiv - a flat preprint
  package (standard article class, inline bibliography, 48 figures). Each
  zip is sealed with SHA-256 checksums and carries its own step-by-step
  submission wizard guide. The study is a numerical and formal
  investigation of a mathematical model; it does not prove the Riemann
  hypothesis - the honesty layer (does_not_prove fields, verdict:
  certified, RH conclusion unlocked) travels with every package. Gate
  ledger of the programme (unified edition, synced 2026-10-16): G1-G5
  YES; blind campaign C17 NEGATIVE by its pre-registered criterion; the
  algebraic_map section closes the pixel encoding exactly in Q.
keywords:
  - Riemann zeta
  - Hilbert-Polya
  - Aharonov-Bohm
  - lattice Dirac operator
  - GUE statistics
  - peer review
  - submission package
